I find skilled/expert is often very handy for hitting bees/ants.  It's
very often a free to-hit bonus and damage bonus early on, when
survivability is lowest.

With priests I'd certainly advance mace to expert unless I get luck
maxed before running into anything tough to hit; they have no missile
weapons they're going to advance and no need for any expert spell
schools (they only get 3 schools anyway).

I'll generally just note when it can be advanced, then if I see
something coming where I think advancing might be remotely useful,
I'll go ahead and advance.

With wizards I'll only take the staff to skilled, and then only if
I've not yet gotten dagger to skilled and/or found a +1 or better
dagger--they really want expert dagger and have a lot of spell schools
to advance.



